title: Seat
---
<<if isTeacherDistracted()>>
    What do you want to do with the teacher distracted?
<<else>>
    What do you want to do during class?
<<endif>>

-> Pump out an essay for Opitz. <<if isTeacherDistracted() and hasActions()>>
    <<jump Essay>>
-> Pay attention. <<if not isTeacherDistracted() and hasActions()>>
    <<jump PayAttention>>
-> Cause a distraction. <<if not isTeacherDistracted() and hasActions() and GetPaper() > 0>>
    <<jump Distraction>>
-> Back
    <<stop>>
===

title: PayAttention
---
You pay attention to the lecture, for about 12 minutes...
<<useAction>>
<<stop>>
===

title: Distraction
---
<<useAction>>

<<if GetTeacherSeesYou()>>
    Teacher: Dude... I can see you. 
    Teacher: Get out of my class.
    <<gameOver>>

<<elseif GetPaper() == 1>>
    You pull out the normal piece of paper.
    Teacher: Bruh...
    Teacher: Get out of my class.
    <<gameOver>>

<<elseif GetPaper() == 2>>
    You pull out the crumpled paper.
    Teacher: WHO THREW THAT?!
    <<PaperDistraction>>
<<endif>>

<<stop>>
===

title: Essay
---
<<useAction>>
You write up an essay to turn into Opitz in exchange for a chapel credit.
That's your first credit gained!

<<stop>>
===

title: Bench
---
Take a quick rest?
-> Yes!
    <<jump Resting>>
-> Nah.
    <<stop>>
===

title: Resting
---
You rest for a while and can no longer enter chapel in time...
<<useAction>>
<<stop>>
===

title: ChapelSeat
---
Sit down for chapel?

-> Yes.
    <<jump Chapel>>
-> Not yet.
    <<stop>>
===

title: Chapel
---
<<useAction>>
You gain a chapel credit for listening!

<<cameraToOpitz>>

Opitz: Welcome to chapel, everyone!
Opitz: Blah blah blah...

<<cameraToPlayer>>

You listen until chapel is over and are let out.

<<nextPeriod>>
<<changeScene "Lunch">>
<<stop>>
===